// Dutch (nl) — Northern Standard Dutch, a cleanroom rule-based g2p. Referees: kaikki nl (PRIMARY, HUMAN, 46.5k)
// + wikipron nld_latn broad (SECONDARY, HUMAN, 45.9k). Both are Wiktionary-derived — a different parsing/coverage
// of the SAME source, so this is weak (same-source) corroboration, not two independent referees; recorded as the
// secondaryGap. Duplicate/variant prons are merged into tab-separated variants (the eval credits any). The
// BACKBONE strips length ː and the offglide ̯, so the surviving signal is vowel QUALITY (aː/ɑ → a/ɑ stays
// contrastive: schwa vs full vowel is the load-bearing distinction) + consonants. Folds are notational only.
{
    "referees": [
        {
            "file": "nl.kaikki-nl.tsv",
            "source": "kaikki nl (Wiktionary, human)",
            "role": "primary"
        },
        {
            "file": "nl.wikipron-nld-broad.tsv",
            "source": "wikipron nld_latn broad (human)",
            "role": "secondary"
        }
    ],
    "secondaryGap": "Both Dutch referees (kaikki, wikipron) are Wiktionary-derived — the same underlying human source parsed two ways, so they are weak (same-source) corroboration rather than two independent referees. No non-Wiktionary Dutch pronunciation corpus is free; epitran nld-Latn is unusable as a referee here because it does NOT reduce unstressed ⟨e⟩ to schwa (water→ʋaːtɛr), the opposite of the truth and of both Wiktionary referees.",
    "folds": [
        {
            "pattern": "β̞",
            "replace": "ʋ",
            "note": "kaikki narrow bilabial-approximant variant of ⟨w⟩ → the labiodental ʋ (notational)"
        }
    ]
}
